# Trivy vulnerability suppressions
# Each entry must document WHY it's suppressed and the remediation path.

# --- ARLogAnalyzer.jar (pre-built Java artifact) ---
# Fix: rebuild JAR with updated org.json ≥ 20230227 and snappy-java ≥ 1.1.10.4.
# Tracked for remediation in a separate ticket before the next production release.

# org.json stack overflow (json-java ≤ 20221018)
CVE-2022-45688
# org.json parser OOM (json-java ≤ 20230227)
CVE-2023-5072
# snappy-java unchecked chunk length → DoS
CVE-2023-34455
# snappy-java chunk length overflow → DoS
CVE-2023-43642

# --- Go stdlib CVEs with no upstream fix ---
# internal/syscall/unix: Root.Chmod symlink follow — no upstream fix available yet.
CVE-2026-32282

# --- Frontend image: npm bundled packages (node:22-alpine) ---
# This CVE is in npm's internal dependency (usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/),
# NOT in the application's own package.json. Not reachable at runtime.
# Fix: upgrade to a future node:22-alpine image that ships npm with picomatch ≥ 4.0.4.

# picomatch: ReDoS via crafted glob pattern (fixed in 4.0.4, 3.0.2, 2.3.2)
CVE-2026-33671

